  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(x=\\dfrac{1-i\\sqrt3}{2},\\) where \\(i=\\sqrt{-1},\\) then \\(\\dfrac{1}{x^2-x}\\) is equal to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1+i\\sqrt3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "-1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Directly, \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^2-x &=\\left(\\frac{1-i\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2\\\\ &\\quad-\\frac{1-i\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\ &=-1. \\end{aligned} \\] Its reciprocal is therefore also \\(-1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Compute \\(x^2-x\\) before taking the reciprocal",
        "The number \\(x\\) satisfies \\(x^2-x+1=0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
